SPEC = {'file': 'cover_viridien_forward_deployed_ai_engineer', 'label': 'Viridien Forward Deployed AI Engineer', 'center': True, 'paras': ["I am writing to apply for the Forward Deployed AI Engineer position in Viridien's AI Lab. I am completing an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London, where a distinction is expected, after a BSc in Biological Sciences at Imperial College London, and I currently work as a Data Analyst Intern at TikTok Shop UK. This role is close to what I have actually done: adapting LLM and retrieval workflows so that they work reliably for the people who depend on them, and measuring whether they actually do.", 'What attracts me most to Viridien is the combination of scientific data and practical AI deployment. Making AI useful in real scientific and enterprise environments needs both an understanding of the domain and careful evaluation and monitoring. I enjoy taking an unclear business problem, identifying what users actually need, and turning it into a workflow that can be tested and improved.', 'Before TikTok I worked as a Data Scientist Intern at DS Digital Technology on a medical AI engagement, where I built Python pipelines that called six LLM APIs with retrieval and multi-step workflows and automated the processing and scoring of over 2,400 records. I designed the evaluation framework around it, a 246-question benchmark and a six-dimension rubric that the client adopted as its acceptance standard, and I co-built a scientifically reviewed knowledge graph and ran blinded A/B tests to measure whether it actually improved output quality. This taught me that how you evaluate an AI system matters as much as how you build it.', 'At TikTok Shop UK I am a Data Analyst Intern, where I analyse merchant and transaction data in SQL and Python and build the KPI frameworks and dashboards that operations, product and commercial teams use to set targets and track initiatives. Alongside my analytical work I built an AI agent that automates repetitive steps of the analytics workflow, which has been adopted by my own team and by partner teams. Building it meant understanding an existing workflow in detail, deciding which steps to automate, and then supporting colleagues as they began to rely on it. I use Claude Code in my development work and review the code it produces rather than accepting it unchecked.', 'On scientific data, my background is direct. At Westlake University I analysed multi-omics data and refactored and parallelised the analysis pipeline in Python and R, cutting processing time by around 60 per cent while adding version-controlled scripts so the work could be reproduced. My undergraduate project analysed hundreds of gigabytes of molecular dynamics output through a Python pipeline. I am comfortable with Python, Docker, Git and Linux, and I have deployed applications.', "Thank you for considering my application. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my LLM, retrieval and evaluation experience could contribute to Viridien's AI Lab. I am happy to work from Crawley."]}
